From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-2: power the Wi-Fi module

The vcc_wifi regulator has no consumer, so the kernel never enables it
and the AIC8800 USB Wi-Fi module does not enumerate. Keep it on.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi	2026-10-23 06:04:15.301817668 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2.dtsi	2026-10-23 06:04:15.333818051 +0000
@@ -94,6 +94,9 @@
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&usb_wifi_pwr>;
 		regulator-name = "vcc_wifi";
+		/* no consumer in the DT: keep the USB Wi-Fi module powered */
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		vin-supply = <&vcc_3v3>;
